1
00:00:00,004 --> 00:00:08,673
Meet Echo Loom: your favorite character, by your side. This demo uses prepared AI responses, portraits, and calendar events.

2
00:00:08,673 --> 00:00:17,575
Start with someone you would love to spend time with. A few details give the character a voice of their own.

3
00:00:17,575 --> 00:00:23,365
Here is Evelyn. Her personality, appearance, and speaking style stay editable as you get to know her.

4
00:00:23,365 --> 00:00:33,396
Give her a face, too. Generate a portrait, preview it, and choose the version you like.

5
00:00:33,396 --> 00:00:48,465
Want a different look? Change her hair color, compare the result, and keep the original within reach.

6
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:56,797
Now, just talk. Evelyn brings the same gentle humor into an ordinary rainy-afternoon conversation.

7
00:00:56,797 --> 00:01:05,184
You can take a moment, share a feeling, or simply enjoy a little company.

8
00:01:05,184 --> 00:01:10,728
Ready to do something together? The story and schedule buttons are right beside your conversation.

9
00:01:10,728 --> 00:01:21,601
Set the scene: old friends, a rainy bookshop, and an evening with nowhere else to be.

10
00:01:21,601 --> 00:01:37,700
Let the scene breathe. Read the narration and dialogue a little at a time, at your own pace.

11
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:50,036
You can speak in your own words. Let us ask what has changed since our last visit.

12
00:01:50,036 --> 00:01:59,049
After a little conversation, the first choice appears. Let us browse the astronomy shelf.

13
00:01:59,049 --> 00:02:07,578
That choice opens a new part of the scene. Next, we will look for the old comet guide.

14
00:02:07,578 --> 00:02:21,458
And you can change your mind. Instead of searching the shelves, let us turn this into a cozy study session.

15
00:02:21,458 --> 00:02:27,770
The direction changes, while the character and relationship stay familiar. We are now studying by the window.

16
00:02:27,770 --> 00:02:42,810
Want a different tone? Rewrite the latest segment to make the conversation more playful.

17
00:02:42,810 --> 00:02:54,761
There is the same study scene, with a little more mischief. Your choices shape how the evening feels.

18
00:02:54,761 --> 00:03:00,646
When you return to chat, the story stays here as a saved card. You can pick it up again later.

19
00:03:00,646 --> 00:03:05,910
Now, bring a little of everyday life into the conversation. Choose Sync my schedule.

20
00:03:05,910 --> 00:03:13,970
Connect a read-only calendar. This recording uses simulated consent and a sample physics exam, with no real Google account.

21
00:03:13,970 --> 00:03:21,030
The connection starts a conversation right away. Evelyn acknowledges the calendar and asks about the exam next week.

22
00:03:21,030 --> 00:03:32,228
Tell her a little more. The schedule provides a starting point; your own words supply the personal details.

23
00:03:32,228 --> 00:03:42,631
Her reply stays curious and in character. A calendar entry becomes a natural conversation, rather than a generic reminder.

24
00:03:42,631 --> 00:03:53,284
Keep going for another turn. You decide what help you want and when you would like to come back.

25
00:03:53,284 --> 00:04:00,617
A shared story, a familiar voice, and a little support for real plans. That is the companion experience we are building.

26
00:04:00,617 --> 00:04:07,533
Echo Loom. Your favorite character, by your side. Come back for the next conversation, or the next little adventure.
